# French Learning Hub — private daily-use settings (template; see docs/DAILY_USE.md).
#
# Copy this file OUTSIDE the repository, keep it private, and fill it in yourself:
#   install -d -m 700 ~/.config/flh
#   install -m 600 scripts/daily/daily.env.example ~/.config/flh/daily.env
#   $EDITOR ~/.config/flh/daily.env
#
# scripts/daily/flh-daily.sh passes this file to `docker compose --env-file` for
# every command, so the same database and providers are used each time. It
# never prints these values. Never commit the filled-in file.
#
# Compose syntax: KEY=value. Put any value containing $, #, spaces or quotes in
# single quotes so it stays literal, e.g. OPENAI_API_KEY='...'.

# ---- Persistent data (required) ----
# Absolute path of an existing private directory (mode 700) owned by FLH_UID.
# It holds app.db. Keep it outside the repository and separate from any
# disposable acceptance session (e.g. ~/flh092-session).
FLH_DATA_DIR=/absolute/path/to/flh-daily-data
FLH_UID=1000
FLH_GID=1000

# Host port, bound to 127.0.0.1 only. Browse remotely through an SSH tunnel.
FLH_HOST_PORT=8080

# ---- Providers (required: state both explicitly) ----
# openai calls the configured OpenAI Responses API when you explicitly request
# an analysis or an extraction; each request may be billed. rule-based / disabled
# keep that step local / off.
AI_PROVIDER=openai
EXTRACTOR_PROVIDER=openai

# Optional (FLH-097): openai enables "Generate suggestions" in Concept Review,
# one explicit, possibly billed request per batch of at most 10 units. Leave it
# disabled (the default) to keep that step off. Suggestions never change a
# membership; only your per-item confirmation does.
SUGGESTION_PROVIDER=disabled

# Optional (Listening v1): openai enables "Prepare exercise" in Listening, one
# explicit, possibly billed request per click over a transcript you supplied.
# Leave it disabled (the default) to keep that step off; saving links and
# transcripts, browsing and opening videos never call a model.
LISTENING_PROVIDER=disabled

# Optional (Reading v1): openai enables "Prepare exercise" in Reading for your
# own passages, one explicit, possibly billed request per click. The authored
# examples, reading, answering and revealing never call a model.
READING_PROVIDER=disabled

# Optional (Writing v1): openai enables "Request feedback" on one draft version
# in Writing, one explicit, possibly billed request per click. Writing,
# revising and comparing drafts never call a model.
WRITING_PROVIDER=disabled

# Your own choices. Both are required when either provider is openai.
OPENAI_MODEL=replace-with-your-model-name
OPENAI_API_KEY='replace-with-your-key'

# Optional: a compatible gateway instead of the public API.
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1

# Seconds. Real extraction can take longer than the 8 s default. The provider
# timeout must stay below the HTTP write timeout, or a stored result can reach
# the browser as a lost response (shown as an unknown outcome).
OPENAI_TIMEOUT=60
HTTP_WRITE_TIMEOUT=75

# ---- Optional: Daily Listening (docs/DAILY_USE.md §10) ----
# Every part is off unless enabled here. A pull runs only when you press
# "Pull now" in Listening or run `flh-daily.sh listening-pull` (for example from
# the systemd timer in scripts/daily/systemd/, which you install yourself).
#
# Read one YouTube playlist's official metadata (video ID, title, date) with the
# YouTube Data API. New videos wait for your transcript; nothing is downloaded,
# scraped or transcribed.
LISTENING_PLAYLIST_SOURCE=disabled
# LISTENING_PLAYLIST_ID=PLreplace-with-your-playlist-id
# YOUTUBE_API_KEY='replace-with-your-youtube-data-api-key'
# LISTENING_PLAYLIST_MAX_ITEMS=50
#
# daily: a pull prepares at most ONE lesson per local day, only from playlist
# videos you gave a transcript, with LISTENING_PROVIDER=openai (possibly billed).
# A failed or unknown preparation is never retried by a pull.
LISTENING_AUTO_PREPARE=disabled
# The zone whose calendar day the cap counts (default UTC). Use the same zone
# as the timer's OnCalendar line, e.g. Europe/Paris.
# LISTENING_TIMEZONE=Europe/Paris
#
# telegram: announce a lesson a pull prepared (its title only; never the
# transcript, answers or a link). Needs LISTENING_AUTO_PREPARE=daily.
LISTENING_NOTIFY=disabled
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN='replace-with-your-bot-token'
# TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=replace-with-your-chat-id

# Optional: allow these exact browser origins to send changes (defaults to the
# development origins). Same-origin use through the tunnel needs nothing here.
# HTTP_TRUSTED_ORIGINS=http://127.0.0.1:8080,http://localhost:8080
